	"title": "A mutex as a tank and key",
	"label": "Dimetric water tank on a stand, filled by two pumps, one at each side, each run by its own controller with a key slot on top. Between them a lock box holds a single accented interlock key. Hover or arrow keys lift one part.",
	"caption": "Both controllers want to read the level and run their pump; only the one holding the single key may, so two pumps never fill the tank at once and it never overflows.",
